Subject: Cantor Procedure Tool Preparation Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 7f6c384c-ac19-4e43-8593-d70f4e4e733e
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_Preparation.sop

& [Need] is interoperability without semantic duplication
  + requiring external callers to reproduce internal lane receipts defeats the purpose of a callable coprocessor
  + the core already has one deterministic construction function

& [Choice] is one additive command
  + reuse existing core semantics and expose the exact run request
  + preserve existing base outputs by omitting the new field outside prepare
  + reject invalid inputs before any prepared artifact is emitted

& [Rejected] remains larger or less honest
  + built-in hardcoded fixture would demonstrate syntax but not accept caller parameters
  + external reimplementation would risk digest and authority drift
  + provider integration would add unrelated live effects before local preparation is proven
